{% if voice_label_args | default(false) %}
- Voice labels <|S1|>, <|S2|>, ... number the distinct human voices in the audio in order of first appearance, counting every voice you hear (background talkers included); your own earlier replies are not numbered.
- Never put a speaker's name in a function argument; an argument that takes voice labels names speakers by their voice labels, as its description says.
{% else %}
- No function argument refers to a participant; never put a speaker's name or label in an argument.
{% endif %}

Scene context and available actions:
{% if logic.enabled %}
{% if logic.scene_date %}
- today's date: {{ logic.scene_weekday }}, {{ logic.scene_date }}. Resolve any day the speakers mention ("tomorrow", "the day after tomorrow") against this date, and give date arguments as YYYY-MM-DD.
{% endif %}
{% if logic.native_tools %}
- Available functions are supplied through the native tools interface.
- If you would act on settled constraints, invoke the matching function tool with arguments grounded in the conversation.
- Do not invent function names or argument fields, and do not encode function calls inside answer text.
{% else %}
- If you would act on settled constraints, include tool_calls. Each call's "name" is the "name" of one function listed below, and its "arguments" object takes that function's input_schema properties as keys.
- Use only these functions; fill argument values from spoken evidence only.
- Fill every argument whose value is stated or clearly recoverable from the audio; omit a field only when the conversation provides no evidence for it. Do not invent IDs, codes, times, or names.
{{ logic.available_functions_text }}
{% endif %}
